finding: Light-theme interaction contrast regresses in site/src/chrome.ts: --gold:#d49560 on --bg:#f7f3ec has only 2.30:1 WCAG contrast (sRGB relative-luminance calculation). a:hover applies this to ordinary 16/17px body links and 12px footer links, below 4.5:1; icon/toggle hover and the sole explicit 2px focus-visible outline use the same color, below 3:1 against paper. Thus quiet chrome does not preserve readable links / sufficiently contrasting focus in light mode, despite the browser test passing (it checks outlineStyle != none, not contrast). Independently confirmed those exact CSS values/rules in the running preview HTML. Use an appropriately darker light-theme interactive role (dark theme's existing gold is 7.36:1); retest the affected contrast, not another full browser tier.
